[14:24.83]Recording One
[14:26.77]Let's say you start to brainstorm a list of all the emotions you've ever experienced.
[14:31.89]Just for fun, try it now.
[14:34.22]What's on your list? Chances are,you included things like happy,sad, excited, angry, afraid,grateful, proud, scared, confused,stressed, relaxed and amazed.
[14:50.69]Now sort your list into two categories¡ªpositive emotions and negative emotions.
[14:57.97]Feeling both positive and negative emotions is a natural part of being human.
[15:04.30]We might use the word "negative" to describe more difficult emotions,but it doesn't mean those emotions are bad or we shouldn't have them.
[15:13.33]Still,most people would probably rather feel a positive emotion than a negative one.
[15:19.88]It's likely you'd prefer to feel happy instead of sad,or confident instead of insecure.
[15:26.24]What matters is how our emotions are balanced¡ªhow much of each type of emotion,positive or negative,we experience.
[15:36.30]Negative emotions warn us of threats or challenges that we may need to deal with.
[15:42.13]For example, fear can alert us to possible danger.
[15:46.35]It's a signal that we might need to protect ourselves.
[15:49.74]Angry feelings warn us that someone is stepping on our toes,crossing a boundary,or violating our trust.
[15:57.70]Anger can be a signal that we might need to act on our own behalf.
[16:02.44]Negative emotions focus our awareness.
[16:06.02]They help us to zero in on a problem so we can deal with it.
[16:10.56]But too many negative emotions can make us feel overwhelmed, anxious,exhausted or stressed out.
[16:18.27]When negative emotions are out of balance,problems might seem too big to handle.
[16:24.81]The more we dwell on negative emotions,the more negative we begin to feel.
[16:30.32]Focusing on negativity just keeps it going.
[16:34.26]Positive emotions balance out negative ones,but they have other powerful benefits, too.
[16:41.73]Instead of narrowing our focus like negative emotions do,positive emotions affect our brains in ways that increase our awareness,attention and memory.
[16:52.94]They help us take in more information,hold several ideas in mind at once,and understand how different ideas relate to each other.
[17:03.44]When positive emotions open us up to new possibilities,we are more able to learn and build on our skills.
[17:12.02]That leads to doing better on tasks and tests.
[17:15.94]People who have plenty of positive emotions in their everyday lives tend to be happier,healthier, learn better,and get along well with others.
[17:28.70]Questions 16 to 18 are based on the recording you have just heard.
[17:35.00]16. What does the speaker say about negative emotions?
[17:53.61]17. What happens to people whose negative emotions are out of balance?
[18:12.65]18. How do positive emotions affect us?
